menu "Authenticator clock"

config AUTH_RTC_MAINTENANCE
    bool "Periodic SDK RTC maintenance"
    default y
    depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32C3 && RTC_CLK_SRC_INT_8MD256
    help
        Wake every 900 seconds through the normal SDK startup path, refresh
        the selected RTC source calibration, and return to deep sleep without
        initializing the display, audio, or radios. Observed key activity,
        invalid continuation, and rejected sleep enter the full application.
        Validate key coverage, UTC continuity, and whole-board power on device.

config AUTH_RTC_WAKE_STUB
    bool "Experimental RTC maintenance wake stub"
    default n
    depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32C3 && RTC_CLK_SRC_INT_RC && !AUTH_RTC_MAINTENANCE
    help
        Enable timer-only RTC maintenance with interruptible RC calibration.
        This requires the pinned IDF 5.5.6 RTC/ROM placement audit and on-device
        key-pulse, wake/re-sleep and power acceptance. Keep disabled in an
        ordinary release until those hardware checks pass. GPIO-only sleep
        compensation and normal runtime temperature learning remain available.

endmenu
